    "evaluator_feedback": "```\n[DIAGNOSIS]:\nThe error at line 259, column 30 arises because the set comprehension {d.role | some d: Delegation | ...} is incorrectly formed in Alloy 6. In Alloy 6, set comprehensions using a generator and a filter must use the syntax {d: Delegation | <condition> | <expression>}, where the generator comes first, followed by the filter, and then the result expression. The current code instead places d.role before the generator, which is invalid. The parser expects a generator variable after the '{' and before the '|', not an expression.\n\n[FIX INTENT]:\nRewrite the set comprehension in directRoles so it conforms to valid Alloy 6 comprehension syntax.\n\n[REPAIR INSTRUCTIONS]:\n- Step 1: Locate the function definition for directRoles at line 258.\n- Step 2: Replace the body of the function:\n  From:\n      s.userRoles[u] - {d.role | some d: Delegation | d.to = u and d in s.activeDelegations and d.role = d.role}\n  To:\n      s.userRoles[u] - {d: Delegation | d.to = u and d in s.activeDelegations | d.role}\n  (That is, use the generator form: {d: Delegation | <filter> | <expression>}, so the set comprehension is well-formed.)\n\n[RATIONALE]:\nThis fix uses the correct Alloy 6 comprehension syntax, addressing the root cause (misplaced expression before the generator), and is a different strategy from previous failed attempts which did not address the set comprehension structure.\n\n[LESSON]:\nAlways ensure set comprehensions in Alloy 6 are structured as {generator | filter | result-expression}, never placing the result expression before the generator.\n```",
